      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum of the pyramid, we start by calculating the volumes of both the original pyramid and the smaller pyramid.\n\nFirst, calculate the volume of the original pyramid. The formula for the volume of a pyramid is given by:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} B h \\]\nwhere \\( B \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the pyramid.\n\nThe base of the original pyramid is a square with side length 12 cm, so the area \\( B \\) of the base is:\n\\[ B = 12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\nThe height of the original pyramid is 8 cm, so the volume \\( V_{\\text{original}} \\) is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNext, calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid. The base of the smaller pyramid is a square with side length 6 cm, so the area \\( B \\) of the base is:\n\\[ B = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2 \\]\n\nThe height of the smaller pyramid is 4 cm, so the volume \\( V_{\\text{small}} \\) is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNow, the volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is:\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
