      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the volume of the frustum, we first need to calculate the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid removed in the cut. The formula for the volume of a pyramid is \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height}\\).\n\n1. **Volume of the original pyramid:**\nThe base edge of the original pyramid is 12 cm and its altitude is 8 cm. The base area of the original pyramid is:\n\\[\n12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\nSo, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\n2. **Volume of the smaller pyramid:**\nThe base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm and its altitude is 4 cm. The base area of the smaller pyramid is:\n\\[\n6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\nSo, the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\n3. **Volume of the frustum:**\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[\n384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.",
